WEBVTT

00:00.220 --> 00:03.937
Trust Drop lets you set the ground rules for an encrypted link.

00:03.937 --> 00:08.274
Here’s how to share a sample message with a password and a one-view limit.

00:08.984 --> 00:11.070
Start with a message or file.

00:11.070 --> 00:13.156
I’ll enter a short sample message.

00:14.164 --> 00:18.030
Under Expires In, choose how long the link stays available.

00:18.030 --> 00:20.350
I’ll leave it at twenty-four hours.

00:20.350 --> 00:24.603
Under Max Views Before Burn, choose how many deliveries to allow.

00:24.603 --> 00:26.536
I’ll use one view here.

00:27.246 --> 00:32.168
Add a password for extra protection and share it separately from the link.

00:32.168 --> 00:35.576
Under Wrong Password, choose Burn Immediately or Allow Retry.

00:35.576 --> 00:42.392
A retry is possible only if views remain, because a delivery uses a view even if decryption fails.

00:43.102 --> 00:44.605
Select Create Secure Drop.

00:44.605 --> 00:47.611
Trust Drop encrypts the message in your browser.

00:47.611 --> 00:51.369
Copy the link and send it to the intended recipient.

00:52.079 --> 00:55.992
The recipient enters the password and selects Decrypt Message.

00:55.992 --> 00:58.601
Their browser decrypts the drop locally.

00:59.311 --> 01:01.310
That used the one allowed view.

01:01.310 --> 01:05.310
Open the same link again, and the drop is no longer available.

01:06.880 --> 01:09.504
For a deeper look, visit the How It Works page.

01:09.764 --> 01:13.433
Or go to Trust Drop dot com and create your first drop today.
